// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/compiler/theory/speed_quality.t27 -- compile speed and code quality of t27b and t27c, published as
; numbers against reference compilers: cell C7 of specs/compiler/theory/sieve.t27 (gHashTag/t27#7596).
; The sample constants are TOOL-WRITTEN from the run files; the fns and tests after them are hand-written,
; and the tests recompute every published median and geomean from the samples. ASCII only (L3).
; -- The run --
; Where: the Railway t27b lab (x86_64, AMD EPYC 9655, 48 cores, shared), 2026-10-09 11:32Z-11:50Z, master
; be9757784 (plus the `t27b test --time` print of #7596, which does not change code generation). Nothing
; ran on the Mac. Method of the #6488 comment: 5 repetitions per row, min and median published, the
; 1-minute load average recorded beside every sample.
; What: the six kernels of specs/benchmarks (kernel_<k>.t27, #6568), each a file of `test` blocks. Every
; row compiles the same file and runs all of its tests; every program ran on aarch64 under qemu-aarch64
; 7.2 user mode, so run times are emulated arm64 time, equal across rows, not native speed.
; Rows (run):
;   T27B_WALL  t27b JIT: process wall, compile + run, under qemu
;   T27B_RUN   t27b JIT: run phase only (t27b --time phases)
;   GCC_O0     t27c gen-c + aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc 12.2 -O0
;   GCC_O2     t27c gen-c + gcc -O2
;   CLANG_O0   t27c gen-c + zig cc (clang 21.1.0) -O0, musl
;   CLANG_O2   t27c gen-c + zig cc (clang 21.1.0) -O2, musl
;   ZIG_DEBUG  t27c gen + zig 0.16.0 test -O Debug
;   ZIG_FAST   t27c gen + zig test -O ReleaseFast
; Rows (compile, x86_64 host unless named):
;   C_T27C_GEN_C t27c gen-c, x86 host
;   C_T27C_GEN   t27c gen, x86 host
;   C_T27B_BUILD t27b build (AOT object), x86 host
;   C_T27B_JIT   t27b JIT phases read..jit-map, under qemu
;   C_GCC_O0     gcc -O0
;   C_GCC_O2     gcc -O2
;   C_CLANG_O0   zig cc -O0
;   C_CLANG_O2   zig cc -O2
;   C_ZIG_DEBUG  zig test -O Debug, fresh local cache
;   C_ZIG_FAST   zig test -O ReleaseFast, fresh local cache
; There is no clang on the lab; `zig cc` (clang 21.1.0 inside zig 0.16.0, musl target) is the clang row.
; zig compile rows include building the test runner with a fresh local cache; libc and compiler_rt come
; from a global cache warmed before timing. t27b JIT compile is the sum of its phases before `run`, under
; qemu, so it is not comparable 1:1 with the x86 rows.
; -- Medians, ms (kernels: fib sieve matmul collatz ternary f64loop) --
;   T27B_WALL      421.7   547.5  1257.4  1375.5   486.0   457.6
;   T27B_RUN       359.4   453.5  1125.7  1206.7   378.9   363.8
;   GCC_O0         371.2   475.4   708.8   752.9   339.0   489.7
;   GCC_O2         123.0   241.7   269.1   350.4   210.8   373.5
;   CLANG_O0       408.2  1659.8  3739.2  1617.5  2049.9   400.7
;   CLANG_O2       183.8   394.4   194.7   308.5   148.2    17.4
;   ZIG_DEBUG      522.0  1260.3  2319.4  1953.8   839.8   509.8
;   ZIG_FAST       187.1   303.1    88.8  1532.9   163.1   513.7
;   C_T27C_GEN_C     3.5     3.7     5.7     3.8     4.4     5.5
;   C_T27C_GEN       4.6     5.0     7.9     4.5     4.3     4.1
;   C_T27B_BUILD     2.8     2.9     2.8     2.9     3.2     2.5
;   C_T27B_JIT      32.7    57.1    86.0    42.1    57.7    49.5
;   C_GCC_O0        43.9    54.0    46.2    44.3    45.4    49.3
;   C_GCC_O2        66.3    70.1    77.3    62.0    72.0    51.5
;   C_CLANG_O0      68.4    92.4    96.7    72.1    88.7    77.6
;   C_CLANG_O2      79.6   125.5   123.0    75.0   134.8    66.2
;   C_ZIG_DEBUG   3642.9  3653.8  4592.4  3506.0  3465.6  4739.1
;   C_ZIG_FAST   15842.7 16010.1 16361.5 15037.8 16435.2 15457.3
; Load average during each kernel (min-max): fib 30-46, sieve 35-50, matmul 52-106, collatz 33-52, ternary 28-47, f64loop 43-55.
; JIT image size, words of 4 bytes: fib 121, sieve 353, matmul 713, collatz 145, ternary 789, f64loop 157.
; -- Geometric means of the median ratios (the tests below recompute them) --
;   T27B_WALL  / CLANG_O2        3.131  (5 kernels: f64loop left out, clang -O2 runs it in 17 ms (T753))
;   T27B_RUN   / CLANG_O2        2.648  (same 5 kernels, t27b run phase only)
;   T27B_WALL  / ZIG_FAST        2.271  (all 6 kernels)
;   T27B_RUN   / ZIG_FAST        1.901  (all 6, run phase)
;   T27B_WALL  / GCC_O2          2.717  (all 6)
;   GCC_O2     / CLANG_O2        0.983  (t27c C through the two C compilers)
;   ZIG_DEBUG  / ZIG_FAST        3.542  (t27c Zig, Debug vs ReleaseFast)
;   C_CLANG_O2 / C_T27C_GEN_C   22.241  (C compile vs the t27c front end that wrote the C)
;   C_ZIG_FAST / C_T27B_JIT    306.051  (zig ReleaseFast build vs t27b JIT compile)
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

